{"page": 87, "lines": [{"t": "5.3", "x": 264.0, "y": 189.0}, {"t": "5.4", "x": 258.0, "y": 1026.0}, {"t": "5.4. 1", "x": 253.0, "y": 1871.0}, {"t": "5.4. 2", "x": 251.0, "y": 2235.0}, {"t": "12/91", "x": 251.0, "y": 2518.0}, {"t": "DSP-2232 OPERATING MANUAL", "x": 263.0, "y": 71.0}, {"t": "5-3", "x": 1054.0, "y": 2522.0}, {"t": "MAILDROP OPERATION", "x": 1515.0, "y": 73.0}, {"t": "SYSOP Mail Drop Commands", "x": 469.0, "y": 191.0}, {"t": "While you have logged on to your MailDrop from your local keyboard", "x": 467.0, "y": 268.0}, {"t": "with the MDCHECK command, the commands available to you are:", "x": 467.0, "y": 308.0}, {"t": "These are the \" standard\" BBS commands available to the Mail Drop SYSOP.", "x": 466.0, "y": 469.0}, {"t": "Any other command sent by you is answered with the error message", "x": 465.0, "y": 509.0}, {"t": "A brief description of each command follows. All the", "x": 750.0, "y": 548.0}, {"t": "What?\"", "x": 567.0, "y": 549.0}, {"t": "available commands are described in detail following the next section.", "x": 466.0, "y": 587.0}, {"t": "B", "x": 568.0, "y": 709.0}, {"t": "E", "x": 567.0, "y": 749.0}, {"t": "K", "x": 567.0, "y": 790.0}, {"t": "L", "x": 566.0, "y": 830.0}, {"t": "R", "x": 566.0, "y": 870.0}, {"t": "s", "x": 566.0, "y": 911.0}, {"t": "BYE", "x": 670.0, "y": 710.0}, {"t": "EDIT", "x": 669.0, "y": 750.0}, {"t": "KILL", "x": 669.0, "y": 791.0}, {"t": "LIST", "x": 668.0, "y": 830.0}, {"t": "READ", "x": 668.0, "y": 871.0}, {"t": "SEND", "x": 669.0, "y": 911.0}, {"t": "Log off the Mail Drop", "x": 870.0, "y": 708.0}, {"t": "Edit a MailDrop message", "x": 870.0, "y": 748.0}, {"t": "Kill or delete messages", "x": 870.0, "y": 789.0}, {"t": "List the message directory", "x": 869.0, "y": 829.0}, {"t": "Read a specific message", "x": 870.0, "y": 869.0}, {"t": "Send a message", "x": 870.0, "y": 910.0}, {"t": "Remote User Mail Drop Commands", "x": 461.0, "y": 1028.0}, {"t": "When a remote user has logged on to your Mail Drop the following", "x": 460.0, "y": 1107.0}, {"t": "commands will be available to the distant station:", "x": 461.0, "y": 1149.0}, {"t": "A brief description of each command follows.", "x": 458.0, "y": 1309.0}, {"t": "These Mail Drop commands are described in detail in the next sections.", "x": 458.0, "y": 1348.0}, {"t": "A", "x": 560.0, "y": 1431.0}, {"t": "B", "x": 562.0, "y": 1471.0}, {"t": "H", "x": 561.0, "y": 1511.0}, {"t": "K", "x": 561.0, "y": 1593.0}, {"t": "L", "x": 560.0, "y": 1633.0}, {"t": "R", "x": 560.0, "y": 1674.0}, {"t": "s", "x": 560.0, "y": 1714.0}, {"t": "ABORT", "x": 663.0, "y": 1432.0}, {"t": "BYE", "x": 665.0, "y": 1471.0}, {"t": "HELP", "x": 664.0, "y": 1511.0}, {"t": "JLOG", "x": 663.0, "y": 1552.0}, {"t": "KILL", "x": 664.0, "y": 1593.0}, {"t": "LIST", "x": 663.0, "y": 1633.0}, {"t": "READ", "x": 663.0, "y": 1674.0}, {"t": "SEND", "x": 663.0, "y": 1714.0}, {"t": "VERS ION", "x": 662.0, "y": 1754.0}, {"t": "HELP", "x": 662.0, "y": 1795.0}, {"t": "Aborts the reading of a long message", "x": 867.0, "y": 1430.0}, {"t": "Log off the MailDrop", "x": 868.0, "y": 1470.0}, {"t": "Help for the Mail Drop commands", "x": 867.0, "y": 1510.0}, {"t": "Sends the DSP—2232 MHeard list", "x": 868.0, "y": 1550.0}, {"t": "Kill or delete messages", "x": 867.0, "y": 1592.0}, {"t": "List the message directory", "x": 867.0, "y": 1631.0}, {"t": "Read a specific message", "x": 867.0, "y": 1672.0}, {"t": "Send a message", "x": 867.0, "y": 1713.0}, {"t": "Sends the DSP—2232 sign—on message", "x": 867.0, "y": 1753.0}, {"t": "Help for the MailDrop commands", "x": 866.0, "y": 1793.0}, {"t": "(ABORT) (Remote only)", "x": 502.0, "y": 1874.0}, {"t": "The \"A\" command aborts the Listing or Reading of messages by a calling", "x": 455.0, "y": 1952.0}, {"t": "station. This is handy if the remote user decides not to continue", "x": 456.0, "y": 1993.0}, {"t": "reading a long message. The message \" *** Done\" followed by the", "x": 455.0, "y": 2035.0}, {"t": "Mail Drop prompt will be sent after an Abort has been received. On the", "x": 454.0, "y": 2074.0}, {"t": "local terminal the SYSOP may type the CANLINE character (default", "x": 456.0, "y": 2114.0}, {"t": "<CTRL—X>) to abort a long screen dump.", "x": 454.0, "y": 2157.0}, {"t": "(BYE)", "x": 501.0, "y": 2238.0}, {"t": "The \"B\" command (Host abbreviation B 1) logs the calling station (and", "x": 453.0, "y": 2316.0}, {"t": "you) off the Mail Drop. A calling station will be disconnected; you", "x": 454.0, "y": 2358.0}, {"t": "will see the standard DSP—2232", "x": 453.0, "y": 2399.0}, {"t": "may also simply disconnect.", "x": 453.0, "y": 2441.0}, {"t": "prompt. The calling station", "x": 1235.0, "y": 2399.0}, {"t": "\" cmd : \"", "x": 1095.0, "y": 2401.0}]}